Provenance. The function declarations in src/decls.rs (lowercase C forms), src/decls_upper.rs (UPPERCASE forms) and
src/decls_user_s.rs (the single-precision user-generator entry points) were written from AMD's published documentation, the
"AOCL API Guide" 6.0 (document 68552, dated 2026-11-10), chapter 9 (AOCL-RNG), by separate writer sessions that were given only
that text. They contain function names and C signatures as the guide states them, and nothing else: no header text, no comments,
no macros, no constants, no example code. They are declared from the guide and link-tested against AOCL 6.0.68 on Windows
(tests/link_all_lower.rs, tests/upper_kat.rs); the guide-stated `GET_RNGVERSION` and the trailing-underscore forms are not
exported by those libraries and are not declared. Measured, not guide-stated: the width of `rng_int_t` (4 bytes in the LP64
library, 8 in the ILP64 library; docs/cleanroom/RNG-WIDTH-MEASUREMENT.md), the callback shapes of the single-precision user
generator, and the protocol of the user-generator entry points (the UINI callback must set `state[0] = n`, `lstate >= n + 3`;
docs/cleanroom/types/userinit/USERINIT-MEASUREMENT.md): those entry points are unsafe, link-checked only, and never called by a
test. The authors of this repository (this lane) HAVE read the AOCL headers; the declarations were not written by those sessions.
Guide line numbers for every declaration are in docs/cleanroom/rng_provenance.csv and docs/cleanroom/rng_upper_provenance.csv at
https://github.com/ThinkersJournal/aocl. This crate does not contain, and does not read at build time, any AOCL header.

